@Padramyr
The script call isn't working because it's looking for a variable named lang or en, which probably aren't defined. You should use quotes around the name.
So it would be:
Iavra.l18N.language = "en";

@cedr777
paste the contents of your JSON into the window at this website. It apparently has a formatting error. The page should tell you what line in your file has the issue:
https://jsonlint.com/

@BreakerZero
see my previous post. If the website for JSONLint gives you a line# in error, open the file in Notepad or whatever text editor you have for viewing straight text, and scroll to that line. Odds are you are missing a comma, or have one at the end of a set, that doesn't need to be there, or a missing end or beginning quote or brace or bracket.
The error at startup shown in
@cedr777
's screen shot is common when there is a formatting error in the JSON, which is loaded at start and has to at least be correctly formatted to work. the braces and brackets have to be in pairs, the lists have to be separated by commas. Read through this thread for some of the more common formatting issues...

